# Pacfile — Arch / Omarchy packages
#
# The Linux counterpart to Brewfile.wsl. Arch ships everything in Brewfile.wsl in
# the official repos, so a machine here uses pacman rather than a second Homebrew
# toolchain shadowing /usr/bin. One package per line; blank lines and # comments
# are ignored. install.sh feeds this to `pacman -S --needed`, which is a no-op for
# anything already present.
#
# Omitted on purpose vs Brewfile.wsl:
#   zlib, bzip2, openssl  — pulled in by the base system; not separately needed
#   libomp, openblas      — the macOS build-flag dance in .zshrc is darwin-gated
#   mise, deno, neovim    — Omarchy preinstalls these
#   github-cli            — gh comes from mise here. Installing it from pacman
#                           too would put /usr/bin/gh ahead of the mise shim,
#                           since env-bootstrap appends the shim dir to PATH.

# ===== Core Tools =====
zsh
neovim
git
direnv
mise
starship

